<%# locals: (todo:, ask_if_done: false, next_up: false) %>
<%# One suggested-task checklist chip (plan-approved pattern; Ember
    port/components/hq-todo-task.hbs + port/constants/hq-todo.js). The
    hq-shift Stimulus controller re-derives icon and text styling from the
    data attributes whenever it completes, revives, or ignores a chip —
    paintChip and paintNextChip there must stay in step with the branches
    below.

    Colour follows what is left to do. The completed chip used to be the only
    coloured thing in the row, which pointed the row's whole chroma at the work
    already behind the operator; done and ignored now recede together to muted
    and are told apart by their glyph. The single chip that is next takes the
    same primary as the "Next:" arrow above it, so the spelled-out next action
    and its position in the checklist read as one signal instead of two things
    to reconcile. Everything else open stays plain body colour: still to do,
    but not now. %>
<%
  if todo.ignore
    chip_class = "text-stone-muted"
    icon = fa_icon("ban", :solid)
  elsif todo.completed
    chip_class = "text-stone-muted"
    icon = fa_icon("check", :solid)
  else
    chip_class = [ ("text-primary" if next_up), ("animate-pulse" if todo.blink) ].compact.join(" ")
    icon = fa_icon("circle")
  end
%>
<%= tag.div class: class_names("inline-flex items-center gap-2 me-4 text-base", chip_class),
            data: { hq_shift_target: "todo", task: todo.task, completed: todo.completed, ignore: todo.ignore,
                    blink: todo.blink, ask_if_done: (true if ask_if_done) } do %>
  <%= icon %>
  <span><%= todo.label %></span>
<% end %>
